# Copy to `local.properties` and fill in. That file is gitignored; this one is
# the checked-in record of what belongs in it.
#
# Every key here is also read from the environment if it is not set in
# `local.properties`, which is how CI supplies them. See the "Secrets" block at
# the top of `android/app/build.gradle`.
#
# Android Studio writes `sdk.dir` into `local.properties` as well. That is
# expected — leave it alone.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Maps
#
# Google Maps / Navigation SDK key, injected into AndroidManifest.xml as
# `com.google.android.geo.API_KEY`. Without it the app builds and runs, but
# maps and in-app navigation fail to authorise.
#
# This is an Android *browser/app* key restricted to the package name and
# signing certificate — not the server-side Distance Matrix key from the
# backend's env.
MAPS_API_KEY=AIza...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Signing
#
# The Play upload keystore. All four are required together; with any of them
# missing, `bundleRelease` and `assembleRelease` fail with an explanation and
# debug builds are unaffected.
#
# The store file is resolved relative to the `android/` folder — so a keystore
# at `android/my-release-key.jks` is just its filename here. Absolute paths
# work too.
#
# Never put these in `gradle.properties`: that file is committed.
MYAPP_UPLOAD_STORE_FILE=my-release-key.jks
MYAPP_UPLOAD_KEY_ALIAS=my-key-alias
MYAPP_UPLOAD_STORE_PASSWORD=
MYAPP_UPLOAD_KEY_PASSWORD=
